From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:23:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] speakup: read review characters from the console
 Unicode screen buffer

`get_char` reconstructed a character from the glyph index stored in the
screen cell, by masking the cell to eight bits, folding in the ninth bit
from `vc_hi_font_mask` and calling `inverse_translate`.  A glyph index
identifies a font position, and a console font holds at most 512 glyphs,
so the reconstruction cannot distinguish two code points that the loaded
font maps to one glyph and cannot represent a code point outside the
font at all.

Call `screen_glyph_unicode` instead.  The virtual terminal keeps a
Unicode screen buffer holding the true code point of each cell, and
`screen_glyph_unicode` returns that code point.

A console that holds no Unicode screen buffer is unaffected, because
`screen_glyph_unicode` then falls back to
`inverse_translate(vc, screen_glyph(vc, n * 2), true)`, and
`screen_glyph` applies `vc_hi_font_mask` to build the same nine-bit
glyph index that `get_char` built before this commit.

The virtual terminal allocates the Unicode screen buffer on demand.
`vc_uniscr_check` allocates the Unicode screen buffer when a process
reads `/dev/vcsu`, and when the console displays a double-width or
zero-width character, and refuses to allocate the Unicode screen buffer
when the console is not in UTF-8 mode.

Add a bounds check on the cell index as well.  `get_char` is called with
a position derived from `spk_pos`, and a caller that walks off the
screen previously read a cell outside the console.

Signed-off-by: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/accessibility/speakup/main.c | 23 +++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/main.c b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/main.c
index 2f45782..b54b859 100644
--- a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/main.c
+++ b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/main.c
@@ -459,20 +459,23 @@ static u32 get_char(struct vc_data *vc, u16 *pos, u_char *attribs)
 	u32 ch = ' ';
 
 	if (vc && pos) {
+		long cell = pos - (u16 *)vc->vc_origin;
 		u16 w;
-		u16 c;
 
-		pos = screen_pos(vc, pos - (u16 *)vc->vc_origin, true);
-		w = scr_readw(pos);
-		c = w & 0xff;
+		if (cell < 0 || cell >= (long)vc->vc_rows * vc->vc_cols)
+			return ch;
 
-		if (w & vc->vc_hi_font_mask) {
-			w &= ~vc->vc_hi_font_mask;
-			c |= 0x100;
-		}
-
-		ch = inverse_translate(vc, c, true);
+		w = scr_readw(screen_pos(vc, cell, true));
+		w &= ~vc->vc_hi_font_mask;
 		*attribs = (w & 0xff00) >> 8;
+
+		/*
+		 * screen_glyph_unicode() returns the true code point when the
+		 * console keeps a Unicode screen buffer.  When the console
+		 * keeps no Unicode screen buffer, screen_glyph_unicode()
+		 * back-translates the glyph exactly as Speakup did before.
+		 */
+		ch = screen_glyph_unicode(vc, cell);
 	}
 	return ch;
 }
